# =====================================================================
#  UserExpandsAll.ab
# =====================================================================
#  sentence   User Expand Tree
#  v4         three separate inlined lambdas, one behavior
#               line 769-775   folder context menu "Expand All"
#                              -> expands only that folder's subtree
#               line 846-849   empty-area menu "Expand All"
#                              -> walk(root), every folder
#               (no header button for this)
#  triggers   folder context menu "Expand All" · empty-area context
#             menu "Expand All"
#
#  TWO THINGS worth seeing here.
#
#  1.  the resource is TREE, not FOLDER, even when the menu sat on
#      a folder.  the response the machine routes on is tree.expand.*
#      either way, so the scope does not earn a second step.  it is
#      the act's second resource, carried in the term as `onto` —
#      grammar.ab already allows it:
#
#          step system expand tree onto folder     # scoped, line 769
#          step system expand tree                 # whole, line 846
#
#      one step, one catch, two call sites.  what the panel expanded
#      is in the term; what the machine waits for is not.
#
#  2.  v4 wrote this three times as three anonymous lambdas.  here
#      it is one sentence and one program, because it is one act.

program UserExpandsAll

sentence  User Expand Tree
enter     tree.expand.requested

step system expand tree onto folder
  catch tree.expand.ok goto Redraw
